\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {27}{\ignorespaces Overlapping POVM elements produce graded case probabilities via quantum interference. Born-rule probability densities \(P(c \mid \mitrho ) = \mathrm {Tr}(E_c \mitrho )\) (\autoref {eq:eq-8-1}) plotted for all eight case roles over the one-dimensional cognitive state-space parameter \(\mittheta \). The NOM element is sharply localized (Tr=0.800) while ACC and DAT elements overlap with NOM in the low-\(\mittheta \) region (Tr=0.100 each), creating an interference pattern in the semantic belief space --- a graded proto-role assignment realizing the \([0,1]\)-enrichment of \autoref {sec:enriched-categories} as physical measurement. Non-overlapping (orthogonal) POVM elements would instead yield crisp, deterministic case assignment. Rotation into a different measurement basis (a different quantum reference frame) corresponds to a different alignment system, e.g., ACC \(\to \) ERG. Generated programmatically from \texttt {src/visualization/quantum\_plots.plot\_povm\_probabilities()}.}}{74}{figure.caption.29}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:quantum-povm}{{27}{74}{Overlapping POVM elements produce graded case probabilities via quantum interference. Born-rule probability densities \(P(c \mid \rho ) = \mathrm {Tr}(E_c \rho )\) (\autoref {eq:eq-8-1}) plotted for all eight case roles over the one-dimensional cognitive state-space parameter \(\theta \). The NOM element is sharply localized (Tr=0.800) while ACC and DAT elements overlap with NOM in the low-\(\theta \) region (Tr=0.100 each), creating an interference pattern in the semantic belief space --- a graded proto-role assignment realizing the \([0,1]\)-enrichment of \autoref {sec:enriched-categories} as physical measurement. Non-overlapping (orthogonal) POVM elements would instead yield crisp, deterministic case assignment. Rotation into a different measurement basis (a different quantum reference frame) corresponds to a different alignment system, e.g., ACC \(\to \) ERG. Generated programmatically from \protect \texttt {src/visualization/quantum\_plots.plot\_povm\_probabilities()}}{figure.caption.29}{}}
