\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {28}{\ignorespaces Prompt injection is detectable as a categorical type violation in the case interaction graph. In the legitimate diagram (top), authority flows NOM\ensuremath  {\to }INS\ensuremath  {\to }ACC per \autoref {eq:eq-9-1}. Prompt injection (bottom) inserts a cross-category morphism \(\mitphi \colon  \text  {Webpage}_{\text  {ACC}} \to \text  {Model}_{\text  {INS}}\) --- the mechanism by which passive Data attempts to seize Instrument authority (ACC\(\to \)INS injection, ultimately targeting NOM-level command). The resulting diagram fails to commute, and the adversary's illicit type-reassignment is flagged as a categorical exception by the case-theoretic firewall---transforming prompt injection from an open-ended jailbreak game into a decidable type-checking problem. Generated programmatically from \texttt {src/visualization/security\_plots.plot\_case\_interaction\_graph()}.}}{82}{figure.caption.30}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:security-violations}{{28}{82}{Prompt injection is detectable as a categorical type violation in the case interaction graph. In the legitimate diagram (top), authority flows NOM\texorpdfstring {\ensuremath {\to }}{->}INS\texorpdfstring {\ensuremath {\to }}{->}ACC per \autoref {eq:eq-9-1}. Prompt injection (bottom) inserts a cross-category morphism \(\phi \colon \text {Webpage}_{\text {ACC}} \to \text {Model}_{\text {INS}}\) --- the mechanism by which passive Data attempts to seize Instrument authority (ACC\(\to \)INS injection, ultimately targeting NOM-level command). The resulting diagram fails to commute, and the adversary's illicit type-reassignment is flagged as a categorical exception by the case-theoretic firewall---transforming prompt injection from an open-ended jailbreak game into a decidable type-checking problem. Generated programmatically from \protect \texttt {src/visualization/security\_plots.plot\_case\_interaction\_graph()}}{figure.caption.30}{}}
\citation{arlas2025adversarial}
