\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {29}{\ignorespaces Monoidal-functor diagnostics for a protocol-vs-implementation comparison. \textbf  {Left panel}: the object map \(F\colon  \symcal {C} \to \symcal {D}\) showing a merge of source roles \{ACC, NOM, A\} into target role ERG and \{S, P\} into ABS (ACC\(\to \)NOM collapse flagged as a type violation). \textbf  {Right panel}: tensor-preservation grid \(F(A \otimes B) \stackrel  {?}{\cong } F(A) \otimes F(B)\) --- \textbf  {blue cells marked with a check} preserve the tensor product (safe); \textbf  {orange cells marked with a cross} mark points where tensor preservation fails --- i.e., the implementation merges or reassigns roles in ways the protocol category does not license. Generated by \texttt {src/visualization/security\_plots.plot\_monoidal\_functor\_security()}.}}{83}{figure.caption.31}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:monoidal-functor-security}{{29}{83}{Monoidal-functor diagnostics for a protocol-vs-implementation comparison. \textbf {Left panel}: the object map \(F\colon \mathcal {C} \to \mathcal {D}\) showing a merge of source roles \{ACC, NOM, A\} into target role ERG and \{S, P\} into ABS (ACC\(\to \)NOM collapse flagged as a type violation). \textbf {Right panel}: tensor-preservation grid \(F(A \otimes B) \stackrel {?}{\cong } F(A) \otimes F(B)\) --- \textbf {blue cells marked with a check} preserve the tensor product (safe); \textbf {orange cells marked with a cross} mark points where tensor preservation fails --- i.e., the implementation merges or reassigns roles in ways the protocol category does not license. Generated by \protect \texttt {src/visualization/security\_plots.plot\_monoidal\_functor\_security()}}{figure.caption.31}{}}
